README
======

This suite runs each case/<name>.in through ./rlhc for the host language
encoded in the file name -- the letter between the first and second '-' -- and
compares the result against the .exp beside it. The harness builds rlhc from
the rlhc-*.lm in this directory; see the comment at the top of
test/harness/rlhc.cc for the file name encoding.

Those rlhc-*.lm are a frozen 2019 copy of the translators in src/cgil, not a
second home for them, and the two have diverged by hundreds of lines apiece.
The copy is not maintained, and cgil changes are not meant to be carried over.

The effect is that colm is what this suite measures. The cases, the expected
output and the translator are all fixed, so colm and libcolm are the only
moving parts, and a difference in the emitted text is a change in colm. At
1066 case files this is the largest colm workload in the tree.

The live translators are tested separately, in src/cgil/test, which runs the
current cgil-* binaries over cases/*.ri. The two suites are not redundant:
that one tests cgil, this one tests colm.

Update the expected files here only when a colm change is meant to alter the
output. Regenerating them against the current src/cgil translators would
couple the suite to cgil and lose what it measures.
